Local changes to vendored sources:
- All generated tables were produced with upstream scripts and committed (aliases.inc, entities.inc, autogenerated-element-type.c, libcss autogenerated_*.c).
- libdom/include: parameter names 'namespace' renamed to 'ns_uri' so the headers parse as C++.
- libcss generator inputs kept in libcss/tools_gen/ (not compiled).
- Python generator scripts and Makefiles removed.
- libcss src/parse/mq.c: "(width >= 576px)" (name before value) mirrored the operator the wrong way and read the
  name as the value, so it never matched; ratio values in ranges fixed too.
- libcss src/select/computed.c: min-width/min-height 'auto' is returned as auto (upstream turned it into 0 unless
  the element itself was a flex container); the layout gives flex items their automatic minimum size.
- libcss src/select/unit.c: vh and vw were swapped (1vh was 1% of the viewport's width, 1vw of its height); and
  css_unit_len2css_px no longer rounds the px per unit to a whole number (10vw of a 533px viewport came out 50px,
  1em of a 14.4px font 14px).
- hubbub treebuilder: <source> and <track> are void elements (added to element-type.h / element-type.c by name and
  to in_body.c's void list); before, everything after a <picture>'s first <source> was parsed into it.
- libdom src/events/dispatch.c, events/event_target.c, core/node.c: mutation events (DOMNodeInserted,
  DOMAttrModified, DOMSubtreeModified, ...) are not built or dispatched while no event listener has ever been added
  and the document has no default actions. Quill has no script, so nothing listens; creating and dispatching one
  per inserted node and attribute was a good part of parsing a page and of freeing one.
- libparserutils src/input/filter.c, charset/codecs/codec_utf8.c: UTF-8 in and UTF-8 out with no partial
  sequence pending, runs of ASCII bytes are copied instead of decoded to UCS-4 and encoded back one at a time.
- libcss src/select/select.c (style sharing):
  - an optional handler callback node_attributes_alike (added at the end of css_select_handler in
    include/libcss/select.h) lets a sibling share a style although attribute selectors or presentational hints
    were considered for it; without it any attribute selector prevented sharing, and the UA's [hidden] made that
    every element;
  - a node that shares a style inherits the candidate's taint flags (a later sibling comparing itself with it is
    held to the same checks);
  - at most 8 earlier siblings are tried as candidates (each failure went on to the one before: quadratic).

stb_truetype (third_party/stb, not NetSurf): composite glyph transforms clamp to the vertex type instead of an
out-of-range float -> short conversion (undefined behaviour); asserts are disabled in src/stb_impl.cpp.
